apps/admin: instance admin panel ("God Mode")

  - A React Router app that builds to static files and runs on port 3001 (VITE_ADMIN_BASE_PATH, usually served at /god-mode).
  - It's for whoever runs the Plane installation, not for regular workspace users. Its sections are in admin/app/(all)/(dashboard)/:
    - general: instance name and settings
    - email: SMTP setup
    - authentication: sign-in options, including Google, GitHub, GitLab and Gitea OAuth
    - ai: API keys for AI features
    - image: Unsplash and other image settings
    - workspace: listing and creating workspaces
  - The home route handles first-time instance setup, where the first admin account is created.

  apps/space: public, read-only project views

  - A React Router app with server-side rendering, on port 3002 (VITE_SPACE_BASE_PATH, usually /spaces).
  - When a project is published in Plane, anyone with the link can view its issue board (list, kanban and so on) here without logging in. Depending on the
    publish settings, visitors can also comment, react or vote.
  - There are only a few routes (space/app/routes.ts):
    - /issues/:anchor is the published board, looked up by its public anchor token.
    - /:workspaceSlug/:projectId resolves to that anchor.

  apps/live: real-time collaboration server

  - A Node/Express backend with no UI, built on Hocuspocus (a server for Yjs, the shared-editing library). It powers multi-user editing in Plane's rich-text
    editor, mainly Pages.
  - Editors connect over a WebSocket (/collaboration), and Yjs keeps everyone's copies in sync.
  - extensions/database.ts loads each document's content from the main API and saves changes back as binary, HTML and JSON.
  - extensions/redis.ts uses Redis to keep several live instances in sync, so it can scale horizontally.
  - It also has two helper endpoints: /convert-document (converts between document formats) and /pdf-export.

  How they fit together

  ┌───────┬───────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┐
  │  App  │        Who uses it        │         Talks to         │
  ├───────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ web   │ Workspace members         │ API                      │
  ├───────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ admin │ Instance operator         │ API (instance endpoints) │
  ├───────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ space │ Anonymous public visitors │ API (public endpoints)   │
  ├───────┼───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ live  │ The editor inside web     │ API + Redis              │
  └───────┴───────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┘

  All four depend on the Django API in apps/api. admin, space and web are frontends, and live is a separate backend just for collaborative editing.